     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "I've marked the run as **normal** and recommended **continuing**. There's no data on the sample yet, so nothing so far says whether the material grew.\n\n- **Oxygen in the exhaust:** Purging brought it down from about 28,800 ppm to 11.8 ppm. Since then it has stayed at about 1–6 ppm through the ramp and growth, so the tube is well sealed against air and there's no sign of a leak.\n- **Temperature:** It followed the ramp closely, overshot by about 10 °C when growth started, then settled at 750 °C. Heater power is steady at about 45%, which matches the temperature reading, so the thermocouple doesn't look like it's drifting.\n- **Argon flow:** Steady at about 100 sccm, matching the setpoint.\n\n**Gap:** The growth stage calls for a pressure gauge, and this furnace doesn't have one. The system check says the atmosphere can't be verified at all, which overstates it: the oxygen sensor does confirm the tube is sealed. What no installed sensor would catch is a blocked exhaust or pressure building up in the tube. A pressure reading, from a temporary gauge or a manual check, would settle that.\n\nThe sample will need characterization (for example Raman or optical) after growth before there's any answer on whether the material grew."
     }
